---
import LandingPage from "../layouts/LandingPage.astro";
import { articleJsonLd, faqJsonLd } from "../lib/seo";
import { APP_URL } from "../lib/config";

const UPDATED = "2026-08-18";
const canonical = "/study-partner";
const title = "Find a Study Partner Online: Quiet Accountability, Not Quizzes";
const description =
  "A study partner on Refocus is a silent accountability partner for a timed session — not a subject-matched tutor. Here's how to find a study partner online without turning it into a study group.";

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "What kind of study partner is this?",
    answer:
      "A quiet accountability partner for the session: you each do your own work with someone present. You are not matched by syllabus, you don't swap notes, and you don't quiz each other. If you want a same-exam tutor buddy, that's a different kind of app.",
  },
  {
    question: "How do I find a study partner online without chatting?",
    answer:
      "Join a timed session. Refocus matches you with someone who's also there to study or work. You share one line about your goal, then work quietly against a shared timer. No small talk required.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is a study partner the same as a study buddy for my subject?",
    answer:
      "No. Subject-matched study buddies discuss the material. A Refocus study partner is parallel and silent — closer to sitting next to someone in a library than joining a revision group.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can I keep the same study partner?",
    answer:
      "Yes. After a session you can add them as a friend and book again. You can also get matched with someone new each time if you just need company for this block.",
  },
  {
    question: "Do we have to be on camera?",
    answer:
      "Cameras stay on for presence so you both know someone is there. Mics stay quiet. The partner is there so you start and stay — not so they can watch over you. You can turn your camera off anytime if you prefer.",
  },
];

const article = articleJsonLd({
  headline: title,
  description,
  path: canonical,
  dateModified: UPDATED,
});
---

<LandingPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  eyebrow="Guide"
  heading="Find a study partner online — quiet company, not a study group"
  lead="Most 'find a study partner' apps match you by subject so you can talk through the syllabus. That's useful. It isn't what Refocus is. Here a study partner is someone who sits with you for a timed block while you both work."
  updated={UPDATED}
  faqs={faqs}
  ctaTitle="Get matched with a study partner"
  ctaText="Pick 25, 50, or 75 minutes. Refocus pairs you with someone who's also there to focus. Share a one-line goal, work quietly, check in at the end. Free to start."
  ctaHref={`${APP_URL}/auth/sign-up`}
  ctaLabel="Start a free session"
  jsonLd={[article, faqJsonLd(faqs)]}
>
  <h2>The two kinds of study partner (don't mix them up)</h2>
  <p>
    Search "study partner" and you'll land on matching apps: same exam, same
    chapter, chat and video to quiz each other. That's a <em>collaborative</em>
    buddy. A <strong>quiet study partner</strong> is the other kind — someone
    present so you actually sit down. They don't help with the problem set. They
    don't need to be on your syllabus. Their job is to be there, working too.
    That's <a href="/body-doubling">body doubling</a>, not tutoring.
  </p>

  <h2>Why silent partners work when groups don't</h2>
  <p>
    Study groups slide into conversation. Subject-matched buddies can become
    another obligation. A silent partner keeps the social pressure that makes a
    library work, without the discussion. You get accountability for showing up
    — which is usually the hard part of long prep — and you keep your own plan.
    We've written more about
    <a href="/blog/silent-co-studying-vs-study-groups">silent co-studying vs study groups</a>
    if that distinction is what you're after.
  </p>

  <h2>How matching works here</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Book a 25, 50, or 75-minute session.</li>
    <li>Get paired with someone else who booked the same window.</li>
    <li>Say what you'll study or work on — one line.</li>
    <li>Work in parallel. Cameras on for presence, muted mics.</li>
    <li>Check in at the end. Add them as a friend if you want a regular.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Want the room framing instead of the person? See
    <a href="/focus-room">online focus room</a>. Grinding UPSC, JEE, NEET, or
    CA? Use <a href="/study-with-me">study together online</a> for exam-prep
    structure. Remote desk work is
    <a href="/virtual-coworking">virtual coworking</a>.
  </p>
</LandingPage>
